;; Changed by Claude, 2026-10-22, for doc/developer/vms-memory.md step 1;
;; reviewed by the user, 2026-10-22, with step 3 and again after step 3
;; was dropped (its ChunkAllocate and ChunkFree gone). What changed, from
;; rtl/vax/GarbageCollectedHeap.Mod:
;; - TagOf (an object's tag, the word before it, by GetWord) and
;;   Census (EnterHeap, CollectNow, then each chunk's blocks from its
;;   first block to its bump pointer, read by ChunkField, each by its
;;   header: for a block in use, IsInUse, the visitor, CALLG (R2) after
;;   the NIL check, with the block's tag word, header DIV sizeUnit (the
;;   floor DIV sequence) and BlockBytesOf(header); then LeaveHeap and
;;   RunPending). Census's labels push every later label up by 10.
;; - The line numbers after them, and the module's key (.IDENT and
;;   POC_K1_...), are new.
;; The file as the user reviewed it before:
;; Written by Claude, 2026-10-14, for Phase 17 (design section 20,
;; proposal 8, approved by the user); reviewed by the user, 2026-10-14. It
;; replaces the file the user reviewed on 2026-10-10. Why this is right:
;; - Each of the 3 FOR loops ends before a step that would pass its
;;   final value (proposal 8), as on LLVM: after the body, SUBx3 at the
;;   variable's width computes the distance left (the final value less
;;   the variable counting up, the variable less the final value
;;   counting down), CMPx compares it with the step's size, and BGEQU
;;   goes on to the step, else JMP L^ leaves the loop. Each adds one
;;   label, so the labels after each are numbered one more.
;; The rest is as the user reviewed it on 2026-10-10:
;; - rtl/llvm's collector, its procedures and their order unchanged,
;;   compiled with SYSTEM.ADDRESS a longword: word, which the body sets
;;   to 4, and every address and size a longword.
;; - What it takes from the system comes from rtl/vax/PocRtl.mar, by
;;   ["VMS"] externals called with CALLG, each argument a longword:
;;   POC_GET_MEMORY(bytes) for calloc, CAllocate multiplying count by
;;   size (MULL3); POC_FREE_MEMORY(address, bytes) for free, CFree given
;;   a table's old size, its capacity read before it is replaced, or a
;;   chunk's bytes + 16; POC_ROOT_TABLES for ModuleTable,
;;   MarkFromModuleTables reading each table's link at 0, its count at 4
;;   and the address of each pointer at 8 + 4i, then the pointer there
;;   (GetWord twice); POC_PAGE_FILE_LEFT for the ceiling.
;; - SYSTEM.GET and SYSTEM.PUT move the address to R0, then MOVL or, for
;;   a CHAR, MOVB between (R0) and the variable; GetByte's result is
;;   zero-extended (MOVZBL). SYSTEM.ADR(marker) is MOVAB -4(FP),
;;   MarkFromStack's and FinalizeAtExit's local. SYSTEM.VAL between
;;   SYSTEM.PTR and SYSTEM.ADDRESS is a longword moved as it is.
;; - Collect passes MarkFromStack, its local label's address (MOVAB), to
;;   POC_SAVE_REGISTERS, whose entry mask saves R2-R11 in a frame
;;   between the scan's start and the base before it calls
;;   MarkFromStack. RegisterFinalizer passes FinalizeAtExit to
;;   POC_AT_EXIT once, as $DCLEXH's handler. A finalizer is called
;;   through its procedure value (FinalizeLast: CALLG list, (R2)),
;;   checked for NIL first (trap 4).
;; - DIV and MOD floor, as everywhere: DIVL3, then the correction when
;;   the remainder's sign differs from the divisor's.
;; - The body sets word to 4, orderBias to ^X80000000 by doubling 1
;;   until it is not positive (MULL2 wraps, the IV bit clear in the
;;   mask), heapLimit to three quarters of POC_PAGE_FILE_LEFT's bytes
;;   (DIVL3 #4, then MULL3 #3), or 1 GB when that is 0, chunkBytes to
;;   256 KB and the mark stack to 16384 entries.
;; - Under -O2 an INTEGER is a word (ChunkField's field, CVTWL 8(AP))
;;   and collections a longword; under -OC, not written here, they are a
;;   longword and a quadword.
;; - On the guest (test.sh), CollectOut, built with -O2 and -OC, prints
;;   output.expected, as the LLVM backend's does: 40 MB allocated with a
;;   heap under 2 MB; lists held by a module variable, a local and an
;;   array of pointers whole, after a mark stack of four entries
;;   overflows; ten finalizers run; NEW giving NIL under a ceiling, and
;;   allocating again once the list is dropped. HeapCeiling's heap stops
;;   between half and three quarters of the paging file quota left.
;; Updated by Claude, 2026-10-15, for Phase 17 step 6 (design section
;; 22.3, proposal 2, approved by the user), for the user's review: the
;; heap disables ASTs while it works, once AsynchronousTraps is
;; initialized. New: the variable astsPossible (a byte); the externals
;; SYS$SETAST and LIB$AST_IN_PROG, called by CALLG; EnterHeap ($SETAST 0
;; when astsPossible, returning whether delivery was enabled, SS$_WASSET)
;; and LeaveHeap ($SETAST 1 only then); MayFinalize (not at AST level,
;; LIB$AST_IN_PROG); Allocate and Collect wrapping AllocateNow and
;; CollectNow between them, then RunPending if MayFinalize; FinalizeLast,
;; taking a table's last entry inside the bracket and calling its
;; finalizer outside it; RegisterFinalizer bracketed; and ExpectAsts,
;; which sets astsPossible. Then (section 22.7, approved by the user):
;; the variable inHeap (a byte); EnterHeap tests it after $SETAST and
;; traps if it is set (POC_TRAP, CALLG with four longwords, 15 and three
;; zeros), then sets it, and LeaveHeap clears it before $SETAST 1;
;; FinalizeAtExit clears it first. So the module's key (.IDENT), its line
;; numbers and its labels after the first new procedure change; the rest
;; is as reviewed before:
